    {
      "id": "ISV-01",
      "title": "The finite Satake scalar on the induced spherical line",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-satake",
      "statement": "For an unramified anti-diagonal unitary group of rank n over the complete valued field, with integral subgroup K, let m=floor(n/2) and α lie in (ℂ×)^m. There is a unique normalized right-K-invariant function φ with the prescribed triangular transformation law. If xK has triangular exponent vector a, its value is Aα(a)=∏_{i=0}^{m−1} αᵢ^{aᵢ}q^{−(n−1−2i)aᵢ}. For a bi-K-invariant Hecke test h supported on finitely many double classes, right translation gives T_h φ=Satα(h)φ, where Satα(h) groups the finite sum at the identity by these exponent vectors.",
      "dependencies": [],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-inert-satake-action",
        "lifts-inert-satake-weight",
        "lifts-inert-satake-scalar"
      ],
