      "status": "source-checked",
      "correspondence": "SphericalExistsU is realized by fixing the triangular part of an Iwasawa factorization. The proof compares two factorizations in B∩K. The Satake eigenfunction theorem uses finite support and the unique exponent vector of a torus cell, then applies the same uniqueness to T_h φ. The variable of the analytic doubling section does not occur in this computation.",
      "review": "Checked the weight with zero-based indexing, class existence and uniqueness, covariance under right-coset reindexing and the actual Satake call in the pointwise integrand supplier."
    },
    {
      "id": "ISV-02",
      "title": "Recovering the zonal coefficient from double-class averages",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-satake-coefficient",
      "statement": "Let c(g)=ℓ(ρ(g)v), with v a K-fixed simultaneous Satake eigenvector of parameter α and with c left K-invariant. At the identity, T_h c(1)=Satα(h)c(1). If c(1)=0 then c is identically zero. Otherwise c(g)/c(1)=|D/K|⁻¹∑_{xK⊂D}φ(x) for D=KgK. The infinite weighted sum then uses |y|<1 and |yαᵢ|, |y/αᵢ|<1; its normalization restores c(1).",
