      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "Applying the linear functional to the finite Hecke-vector sum transfers the eigenvalue to the coefficient at the identity. With an indicator, bi-invariance and a nonempty finite fiber give a nonzero integer multiple of c(g), proving the zero branch as well. The nonzero branch normalizes before applying the integral formula and scales back after it.",
      "review": "A second reader checked the invariance condition on c, the positive double-class count proving vanishing, and that the analytic domain is used only after division by a nonzero c(1)."
