    {
      "id": "ISV-03",
      "title": "Twelve cosets in a single rank-two test",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-satake-example",
      "statement": "In the rank-two anti-diagonal unitary group over ℚ₃(i), D=K diag(3,1/3) K has twelve cosets xK. They have torus exponents 1,0,−1 with multiplicities 9,2,1. The value of the indicator under the Satake character is 3α+2+3/α, and at α=1 the normalized zonal value on D is 2/3.",
